# UNION

The **UNION** operator combines the results of two or more SELECT statements.

It **removes duplicate records**.

### Syntax

```sql
SELECT Name FROM Employee
UNION
SELECT Name FROM Manager;
```

---

# UNION ALL

The **UNION ALL** operator combines results but **keeps duplicate records**.

### Syntax

```sql
SELECT Name FROM Employee
UNION ALL
SELECT Name FROM Manager;
```

---

# Difference Between UNION and UNION ALL

| UNION | UNION ALL |
|--------|-----------|
| Removes duplicate records | Keeps duplicate records |
| Slightly slower | Faster |
| Returns unique rows | Returns all rows |

